      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-09_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <p>Warrington Choirs' Success. The two leading Warrington male voice choir figured at the Preston Musical Festival on Saturday, being placed: Warrington Male Voice Choir third prize and Warrington Apollo Choir fourth in the Male Voice Choir competition.—The adjudica- -tors were Dr McNanght and Mr. Dan Price, A-R.C3I There wasla total of 215 marks for the three pieces selected for competition, the Habergham Choir being placed first, with 221 marks; Southport, second with 219 and Warrington male voice third with 215; the Warrington Apollo Choir being credited with fourth place, with 203 marks. There were three difficult test pieces. It is gratifying to note that the Warrington Male Voice Choir has had a successful year, having won five first ptizes, an the above third, out of the seven competitions in which they have taken part, the total wins amounting to upwards of £BO and trophies.</p>
      </div>
