        <p>The fault of the Blood—that is the direct cause of Rheumatism in every form; and as the disease proceeds irom the blood the only way to a cure is by renewing :the blood supply. That is why Dr. Williams' Pink Pills /or Pale People are so eminently successful in Rheu- matism and other blood disorders, because they actually 'maim strong red blood that cleanses tbe system of poisons and builds up health anew with full relief from</p>
        <p>"All my joints were inflamed with Rheumatism four years ago," said Mrs. Burdin, of 50, Archdeacon-lane, Leicester, when interviewed recently, "and from a :strong active woman I dwindled away to a pitiable wreck, unable to do anything in the THESE WERE house. What I suffered will be HER SYMPTOMS, partly understood when I tell you that agonising pains flew through Illy back and limbs as though my muscles were gripped by pincers, while an icy feeling crept down my spine. My flesh and bones became sore, and I felt as though I had been beaten all over. -</p>
        <p>"Every change in the weather set up fresh attacks and increased my pain. Sometimes I could hardly drag one ,foot after the other, and in time I became quite a cripple. Then rheumatic fever developed, and I had to take to my bed, where for fourteen weeks I lay in agony. Every movement of my body caused excruciat- ing pains to shoot through me; my body twitched with agony, for it seemed as though I was being stabbed with red-hot needles.</p>
        <p>"My fingers became knotted and. my skin puffed ; also, my flesh was so tender that I could not bear the weight of the bed clothes, and I had to have supports to save them from touching me. My breathing became short and sharp, and my heart palpitated. I grew as weak and helpless as a child, and terribly• emaciated, with my nerves in such a bad state that I could not stand the daylight, and the room was kept darkened. "In spite of all the clever treatment of doctors I seemed to get Worse; the medicine they gave me pro- duced nausea, without relieving my agony. "But at this time my husband was strongly advised to give me Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, and though I fully believed I %vas beyond cure, I con- sented to try the pills. After a steady course of the pills I was pleased to notice a decided improvement; I .continued, and the pains began surely te diminish; before long I could move my hands. "This encouraged me so much that I persevered, with Dr. Williams Pink Pills; then my strength returned until I was able to sit up in bed; began to put on flesh; I gradually regained the use of my limbs, and was able to venture out of bed. "Form the time I began Dr. Williams' Pink Pills I' never looked back ; they alone restored me from a hope- less cripple to the strong, healthy wornaa you now see. I am quite free from all pains of Rheumatism and well able to attend to my domestic duties. Dr. Williams' Pink Pills are truly a wonderful medicine. and I cannot praise them too much, for I consider they saved my life." By supplying Red, Good Blood that fortifies the system and drives out all the poisons that set up Rheumatism, innumerable cures have been achieved• by Dr. Williams' Pink Pills for Pale People, which have also cured Antemia, Indigestion, Eczema, Sciatica, St. Vitus' Dance. Neuralgia, Nervous Disorders, Paralysis, and Locomotor Ataxy. Sold at shops (but avoid substitutes, and take care that the full name, Dr. 'Williams' Pink Pill.; fnr Pale People, is on every "/ y • . package), or direct from 7, the British Depot, 46, Holborn-viaduct, London, PaR post free for 2s. 9d. a L Ali a box, or six boxes for tt LE.. .4'44 13 9d s. .</p>
