      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-09_WidnesExaminer_art0042" n="art0042">
        <head>LONELY WIDOW BURNT.</head>
        <p>LONELY WIDOW BURNT.</p>
        <p>Str Rllfa, a widoiv. who iniiste.l on living alone Nowbury, was on Tuesday, burnt to death. Taking a candle to go to bed, she fell at the top of the stairs. Her clothes caught fire, and she died in terrible agony. Her son, calling in the morning, found her charred remains.</p>
        <p>In the le of Wight primroses picked in the open are being offered for sale. A youth named Major Dix was accidentally shot while rsbbiting on the Moyns Park estate, Birdbrook, Essex.</p>
