      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-09_WidnesExaminer_art0094" n="art0094">
        <head>INFIRMARY BALL.</head>
        <p>THE INFIRMARY BALL.</p>
        <p>BRILLIANT FUNCTION.</p>
        <p>The ball which is annually held in aid of the funds ! of the Warrington Infirmary ranks am lngst the lead- i • ing society functions of thi town, and Thursday's pro- ceedings were equally as brilliant as any which had I preceded them. The ball room at the Lion 11)te1 had i been lavishly decorated for the occasion by Mr. Ralph [Johnson, Mrs. Henry Greenall, Mrs. W. P. Rylands, I and others, and when the dancing was in progress I the scene presented was an animated and picturesque I one. There was an abundance of flowers and plants which had been sent by Lady Greenall, Mrs. Lyon, Mrs. Parr, Mrs. Henry Greenall, Mrs. Long, and Mrs. I Frost. Mr. Vetter's well-known band was in atten- dance and an attractive programme of 20 dances was submitted. During an interval supper was served, !Mr. Lee's catering,as usual, being entirety satisfactory. I The stewards were : —Lieutenant-Colonel. J. A. Elelsten Major C. J. Steavenson, The King's (Liverpool Regi- ment), Major T. D. Faircl lug!), Captain G-. R. Cros- field, Dr. E. E. Bowden, Mr. John C on, Mr. Henry Greenall, Mr. James Hepherd, Mr. R )ger C. Parr and Dr. R!ginald Smith The following is a list o Ackerley,Miss I Adams' Miss Airey, Miss Airey, Miss Connie Airoy, Miss Lettie Appleton, Capt. F. M. Baines, Mr. C. T. I Bell, Miss J. Blair, Miss L. M. Blair, Mr. H. A. Blair, Mr. G. C. ! Blair, Miss B. Bleckly, Mrs. Wilfred Bleckley, Miss Boumphrey, Mr. J. Bowden, Dr. and Mrs. Broadbent, Miss M. S. Broadbent, Miss M. E. Broadbent, Mr. Edgar Broadbent, Capt. T. M. Bromilow' Mr. A. Burrows, Mr. F. Chapman, Mr. H. R. Cookson, Miss Corbett, Miss Coxon, Mr. John Crosfield, Capt. G. R. Cross' Mr. &amp; Mrs. Shepherd Day, Mr. Thomas Davies, Mt. J. E., Davies, Mr. Leonard G. Dampier,Captain C. F.,R.N. Darley, Miss Darlington, Miss Daunt, Miss Denham, Captain Doyley, Mr. H. H. Dickson, Mrs. A. (Aston) Dickson, Miss Dumbreck, Mr. Dutton, Mr. Norris Dyson, Miss Earwaker, Mrs. Edridge, Majoz (King's Regiment) Edridge, Mrs. Fa irclough, Mr. &amp; Mrs. John Fairclough,Maj or Brereton Fairclough, Mrs. Dutton Fairclough, Mr. Harry Fairclough, Mr. and Mrs. Henry Fairclough, Major J. D. Fairclough, Mr. Lionel Fairolough, Miss Fairclough, Miss Nora Fairhurst, Mr. Frank G. Fairhurst, Miss Fisher, Mr. J. H. Liver-</p>
        <p>f the guests : Hepherd, Mr. and Mrs. James Hepherd, Mr. J. jun. , Hutchinson, Mr. Jones, Miss Madge Jones, Mr. W. Piers Kirkconnel, Mr. &amp; Mrs. H. Lapage, Mr. R. H. Lardner, Mr. (King's) Layton, Mr. A. J. Lee-Jones, Miss Leigh, Mr. •A. Lennox, (Didsbury) Lister-Kaye, Mr. and Mrs. Allan Lister-Kaye, Miss Lister-Kayo, Miss H. Lister-Kaye, Miss R. Litton, Miss J. Mills, Mrs. Monks, Mr. and Mrs. E.W. Monks, Miss Dorothy Mortimer, Mr. &amp; Mrs.H.P. Osborne, Captain Owen, Mr. and Mrs. Segar Owen, Mr. Gooffaey Owen, Mr. Halsall Owen, Miss Ruth Paul, Miss Pigot, the Rev. H. V. and Mrs. Pigot, Miss Pigot, Miss G. Pilkington, Mr. G. Pilkington, Mr. N. Powell, Miss D. Reiss, Mr. Reynolds, Mrs. J. P. Reynolds, Miss Ridgway, Mr. T. Ritchie-Sidney, Miss Robinson Miss K. Haxby Roody, Captain, Aston Halt Roberts, Miss E. C. Rylands, Mr. and Mrs. W. Peter Stevenson, Mrs. C. J. Selby, Dr. and Mrs. (Prodsham) Settle, Miss Simpson, Mr. F. H. (Birk- dale) Smith, Mr. &amp; Mrs. Douglas Smith, Mrs. Reginald Smith; Miss (Lymm) Smith, Miss D. (Lymm) Smith, Miss Silby,(Helsby) Talbot, Mrs. (Aston Hall) Taylor, Mr. H. D. Thynne, Mr. Tillotson, Miss (Bolton) Tinsley, Miss Van-den-Nest, Miss Walker, Miss Whitely, Mr. W. Williamson, Mr. C. L. Williamson, Mr. G. R. Willis, Mrs. F. W. Willis, Miss Cicely D's Woods, Mr. E. Woodward, Miss Winifred (Aston Hall) I Woodward, Miss (Aston Hall) Wright, Mr. E.</p>
        <p>pool' Fletcher, Mr. and Mrs. A. Forwood, Mr. Talbot Fox, Dr. and Mrs. G. J. Gough, Mr. A. Et. C. Gough, Mr. H. F. Greensll, Mr. and Mrs. Henry Greenshields, Mr. Grundy, Mr. T. Milligan Grundy, Miss E. Grundy, Miss Hampshire, Mr. Harrison, Mr. Maesmore Heaton, Mr. S.</p>
