        <p>Tea Party at Stockton Heath. The annual congregational gathering in connection • with St. Thomas' Church was held in the Church Institute on Thursday evening. The proceeding-9 opened with a tea to which about 100 sat down, the lady members of the congregation having charge of - the tables. The Rev. H. A. ffester presided over the concert which followed and there was crowded attendance. The programme had been arranged by Mrs. \V. B. Roberts, and the excellence of the entertainment can be judged from the fact that it included selections by such well-known local artistes as Mrs .A. Booth, Miss Marie Houghton, Mr. J. Rabbitt, Mr. J. W. Bibby, Mr. Victor Roherts, and Mr. K. Johnson.</p>
