        <p>Coughs, Colds, AND CHRONIC CHEST DISEASES. A SPEEDY HOME. CURE. 7, W. LASCELLES-SCOTT, P.N.S°. (LOND.) ANALYST, LITTLE ILFORD, Lecturer on Chemistry and Ily.;t:ene, says in his Certificate of Analysis, "I have p:easure in certifying that in my opinion VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE is an exceptionally pure, safe, aud effective preparation." VENO'S LIGHTNING COUGH CURE Immediately subdues a cold however severe, eases a cough instantly, and heals the mucus surface of the breathing passages. Its delightful balsamic yroperties are most gratifying, nothing could be better and safer for children's coughs, and to the sufferer from chronic chest diseases it is a complete revelation. ARK FOR EING LIGHTNING COUGH CURE The purest and mod 61ic1en5 Remedy procurable for Coughs, Colds, Bronchitis, Asthma, Catarrh, Weak Lungs, &amp; Children's Coughs. Bid., ttli and WO per bottle. N all Chemists and Drug Stares everywhere. County Court Judge and the Agent. At the Warrington County Court on Thursday, before his Honour Deputy Judge Strathan, K.C., on a judgment stmmons being called, the debtor's wife infortued the Judge that her husband was already committed on two other judgments.—His Honour asked the agent appearing in the case if he knew of that.—The agent replied that he did, and was told so on Monday night.—His Honour asked the agent why he did not give notice to the registrar to withdraw it. —The agent said it was not the custom to do so.—His Honour said that if any agent in the future, when he was sitting, knew of any commitments against any judgment dpbtor who was appearing before him on another judgment summons, and did not withdraw the same by the consent of the Registrar without coming before him (the Judge) he should take serious con- sideration as to whether he would permit such agent to appear before him on a judgment summons in the future. It was only by thelndulgence of the judges that such agents were allowed to appear at all. He was very emphatic in tbis matter, and he hoped all the agents present would remember what he said.</p>
